-- # Class: WindowsTaskFacet Description: A Windows Task facet is a grouping of characteristics unique to a Windows Task (a process that is scheduled to execute on a Windows operating system by the Windows Task Scheduler). [based on http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/windows/desktop/aa381311(v=vs.85).aspx]
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: account Description: Specifies the account referenced in an event log entry or used to run the scheduled task. See also: http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/windows/desktop/aa381228(v=vs.85).aspx.
--     * Slot: accountLogonType Description: Specifies the security logon method required to run the tasks associated with the account. See also: http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/windows/desktop/aa383013(v=vs.85).aspx.
--     * Slot: accountRunLevel Description: Specifies the permission level of the account that the task will be run at.
--     * Slot: application Description: The application associated with this object.
--     * Slot: exitCode Description: Specifies the last exit code of the scheduled task. See also: http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/windows/desktop/aa381245(v=vs.85).aspx.
--     * Slot: imageName Description: Specifies the image name for the task.
--     * Slot: maxRunTime Description: Specifies the maximum run time of the scheduled task before terminating, in milliseconds. See also: http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/windows/desktop/aa381874(v=vs.85).aspx.
--     * Slot: mostRecentRunTime Description: Specifies the most recent run date/time of this scheduled task. See also: http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/windows/desktop/aa381254(v=vs.85).aspx.
--     * Slot: nextRunTime Description: Specifies the next run date/time of the scheduled task. See also: http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/windows/desktop/aa381257(v=vs.85).aspx.
--     * Slot: observableCreatedTime Description: The date and time at which the observable object being characterized was created. This time pertains to an intrinsic characteristic of the observable object, and would be consistent across independent characterizations or observations of the observable object.
--     * Slot: parameters Description: Specifies the command line parameters used to launch the scheduled task. See also: http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/windows/desktop/aa381875(v=vs.85).aspx.
--     * Slot: priority Description: The priority of the email.
--     * Slot: status Description: Specifies a list of statuses for a given Whois entry.
--     * Slot: taskComment Description: Specifies a comment for the scheduled task. See also: http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/windows/desktop/aa381232(v=vs.85).aspx.
--     * Slot: taskCreator Description: Specifies the name of the creator of the scheduled task. See also: http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/windows/desktop/aa381235(v=vs.85).aspx.
--     * Slot: workItemData Description: Specifies application defined data associated with the scheduled task. See also: http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/windows/desktop/aa381271(v=vs.85).aspx.
--     * Slot: workingDirectory Description: Specifies the working directory for the scheduled task. See also: http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/windows/desktop/aa381878(v=vs.85).aspx.
--     * Slot: type Description: The class the thing is an instance of, as the class's CURIE, such as uco-observable:File.
